WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.455
I run an online marketplace so we're
taking payments from customers and then

00:00:03.455 --> 00:00:04.000
passing that

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
money on to people providing the service.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
I genuinely thought we had the payment
side sorted.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.610
Everything seemed to be working, so
honestly I hadn't really given it much

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.000
thought.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.727
I went with Andy and the team because they
insisted on properly auditing our setup

00:00:17.727 --> 00:00:18.000
before

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
we went any further.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.000
And thank goodness they did.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.422
They found an issue with how we were
handling other people's money that could

00:00:24.422 --> 00:00:25.000
have resulted

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
in our payment provider freezing their
account.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
There was also a licensing and
classification issue

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
I didn't even know existed.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
They called it before we properly launched

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.000
and restructured how the money moves.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.000
So now everything's set up the way it
should be.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Was it worth it?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Absolutely.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.000
That one issue could have bought

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
the whole marketplace to a halt.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.106
If you're taking payments, I'd definitely
get your setup checked before you start

00:00:51.106 --> 00:00:51.709
scaling.
